  const { isAdmin, session } = await verifyAdmin();

  if (!isAdmin) {
    forbidden();
  }

  return (
    // ... content
  );
}
```
This is correct.

I'm ready. I will delete the `app/forbidden.tsx` styling and use `app/admin/forbidden.tsx` IF I wanted scoped, but `app/forbidden.tsx` is better for global. The user asked for "a nice error page" for the admin check specifically, but `app/forbidden.tsx` handles `forbidden()` calls globally which is standard.

One minor point: `app/forbidden.tsx` is created at the root of `app`. This handles *any* `forbidden()` call within `app`. This is the correct place for a general forbidden page.

I'll double check if `app/not-found.tsx` exists, just for consistency. I see `/_not-found` in build output, likely default.

I'm confident. I'll provide a summary of changes.

